Package: terminal-system
Version: 1.1.6
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash, tmux
Recommends: xclip
Maintainer: Franco Conidi aka edmond <fconidi@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://www.syslinuxos.com
Description: AI-assisted two-panel terminal (natural language -> shell commands)
 A tmux two-panel layout: the right panel takes instructions in natural
 language, an AI engine (Claude Code or Codex, called non-interactively
 and with no tool access of its own) translates each instruction into
 shell command(s), and those commands are typed into the left panel in
 real time.
 .
 Every command is confirmed manually by default; an opt-in auto-mode
 (":auto readonly") executes only commands that pass a fixed allowlist of
 read-only programs with no shell metacharacters, plus a denylist of
 always-dangerous patterns (rm -rf /, mkfs, dd onto /dev, fork bombs, and
 similar) as a second layer -- anything else always stops for
 confirmation.
 .
 Session instructions and left-panel output are kept as AI context only
 if explicitly enabled (":context on"; off by default), are scanned for
 common secret patterns first, and are never written to disk.
 .
 Requires the "claude" and/or "codex" CLI to already be installed and
 authenticated; neither is a hard package dependency since neither ships
 as a .deb on this system.
Installed-Size: 136
